## 6. SSR and SEO

SEO is a critical business requirement.

The homepage must be search-engine friendly.

Implement and verify:

- Server-rendered or prerendered HTML
- Proper document title
- Meta description
- Canonical URL: `https://tinkerindex.io/`
- Open Graph metadata
- Social sharing metadata
- Semantic HTML
- Proper heading hierarchy
- Accessible navigation
- Appropriate robots handling for development environments

**Important architectural consideration:**

The Angular application currently uses prerendering.

Evaluate whether prerendering or SSR is more appropriate for the homepage.

Ensure the build process does not unnecessarily depend on the development PostgreSQL database or the Mac mini being available.

Use supported Angular SSR/hydration capabilities.

Avoid duplicate API requests during hydration.

Do not introduce custom HTML metadata injection.

Dynamic project SEO belongs to Milestone 3b.

## 7. API Integration

Use existing NestJS endpoints.

Requirements:

- Configurable API base URL
- Typed HTTP responses
- Proper loading states
- Graceful error handling
- Empty-state handling
- No database access from Angular
- No secrets exposed to the browser

Ensure the approach works with both local development and eventual Railway deployment.

Document any configuration changes.

## 8. Performance

Prioritize:

- Excellent Core Web Vitals
- Minimal JavaScript
- Small production bundles
- Responsive layouts
- No unnecessary third-party libraries
- Avoiding cumulative layout shifts
- Lazy-loading noncritical assets
- Accessible focus states
- Reduced-motion preferences

Do not introduce new image infrastructure in this milestone.

